Visual reference
----------------
The pebble-map look (a weighted Voronoi "power diagram" of rounded stones on a
warm sand ground, with raked rings for free space) was inspired by the public
website kanso.botiverse.build (Kanso, by Botiverse, Inc.), viewed on 2026-11-05.

What we checked on that site (2026-11-05):
- The site footer reads "(c) 2026 Botiverse, Inc." and links Privacy, Terms and
  "Open source licenses".
- /terms/ ("Last updated: November 2, 2026") grants use of the Kanso app on Macs
  you own or control, forbids reselling it or removing its notices, and says
  bundled open source components keep their own licenses.
- /licenses.txt lists third-party components shipped inside Kanso (for example
  @agentclientprotocol/sdk, Apache-2.0). It does not license Kanso's own code,
  artwork or website design.
- No LICENSE file is published at the site root (/LICENSE and /license return 404).

Conclusion: Kanso's code, screenshots, icon and site design are not open source
and are not licensed to us. Rake does not copy any of them. No file, image,
stylesheet, script or text from that site is included in this repository. The
pebble map, its geometry code (written from scratch, citing Nocaj & Brandes 2012
for the weighted Voronoi bound), colors and copy are original work under MIT.
An overall visual idea is not something we redistribute; we credit it here as a
courtesy and keep the product name out of the code and copy.

Third-party code
----------------
None. Rake uses only Apple system frameworks (Foundation, SwiftUI, AppKit,
WebKit) and the Swift standard library. Tests use swift-testing, which ships
with the Swift toolchain.
